      "id": 226547,
      "name": "Dandolo",
      "username": "Dandolo",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dandolo/{size}/1845_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-04-19T19:44:55.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>In my first few games since the digital version came out, I was randomizing starting teams and choosing replacement heroes based on what rewards they would inherit and what shield Oblivaeon had out.</p>\n<p>After a while this lead to me playing similar heroes in similar situations, which was effective but not great for replay value. So I switched to using choosing all heroes at random regardless of the situation. It definitely makes the game a lot harder but I think I'm at around a 75% win rate, and I've found alot of really interesting combinations I'd never have otherwise thought of.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:00:30.991Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
