    {
      "id": 226551,
      "name": "FrivYeti",
      "username": "FrivYeti",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-04-23T04:17:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chilly Steke\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Chilly Steke:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I like opening with TN Bunker, so that when he dies, Luminary or Tachyon or Comodora can take his place and use his incap ability “Put deck in trash”. RK Voss does not like getting hit with a fully powered orbital death laser, let me tell ya.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The particularly ludicrous version of that is to use Freedom Five Tachyon and get the Oblivaeon Shard on her. Then, every turn she can move every burst card from her trash into her deck, hitting someone 16-18&nbsp;times for (1+Devastation Tokens) damage each time. It could be more, but you will really want a lot of Syaptic Interruptions there to keep Tachyon from dying in the process.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>A slightly less, but still highly, ludicrous version is to have Legacy and Chrono-Ranger backing her up, to use their cards to give her +4 damage per hit. That’s still a respectable 5 damage per burst, and 80 damage per round will really ruin someone’s day.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:00:31.296Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
